---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, GITHUB_URL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`about — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Eleven years of building real products for real users, and the thing Drew found in 2026 that he likes even more: helping non-engineers build with agents. In his own words."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article class="prose">
				<h1>About Me</h1>

				<p>Hi, my name is Drew, and this is my personal website.</p>


				<h2>About my work</h2>

				<p>
					I'm a software engineer because writing software means I have access to
					the longest levers in the history of the world. I've used those levers to:
				</p>

				<ul>
					<li>build a sentient whiteboard</li>
					<li>disambiguate environmental triggers for people with asthma</li>
					<li>find the most interesting sports trivia</li>
					<li>empower teachers to build interactive lessons for students</li>
					<li>organize medical research studies</li>
					<li>train firefighters via vehicle simulations</li>
					<li>level up switch-based communication for people who are quadriplegic</li>
					<li>test advanced drive-assist systems</li>
					<li>find the perfect camping spot</li>
				</ul>

				<p>
					I've spent the last eleven years building real products for real users
					(I left a bunch out of that list because it was getting long), because
					that's what I've enjoyed most: putting powerful tools in the hands of
					people who need them.
				</p>

				<p>
					In 2026, I discovered something I like even more: helping non-engineers
					learn the craft of building products with the aid of agents and LLMs.
					Alongside my colleagues Aly and Sarah, I founded [gōgy](http://gogylesson.com), a lesson platform
					built by teachers. I designed the software factory and set up the guardrails, and guided architecture and infra decisions
					that enabled them to build safely and ambitiously with Claude Code, without knowing
					how to read code!
				</p>

				<p>
					I think this is the way of the future: ambitious people working with just
					enough engineering guidance to build amazing things. If that sounds
					interesting to you, drop me a line at drewhoover at \\<the email domain that rhymes with 'e snail' \\>.
					<a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>.
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.prose {
		max-width: 62ch;
	}
</style>
